# Chroma library, modern Earth: bold ways, batch 2 (stage A, 2026-10-18). Played lives only (compiled into earth_play.py).
# Each life event below has a first bold way, sometimes a second, and two links (well and badly) on the first, each link
# with its own bold way. Syntax: header of build.py; design: the writer's brief for bold ways.

# ================================================================ a parent dies

== bold: a parent dies / U
base: ask every question about how and why they died, until it makes sense
likelier_if: has [finding things out] +10; has [graduate] +5
- U | ask the hospital for every record, and a meeting on what went wrong | v: universalism, self-direction | act: ask the hospital for every record, and a meeting on what went wrong | chance: 40 | grants: handling red tape | takes_if_fails: family who will always take you in
works: {N} learns every form and every office on the way, and in the end the hospital sits down with the family and answers.
works: The meeting is long and hard, but {N} comes out knowing how {parent} died, and knowing how to make an office answer a letter.
fails: The hospital finds nothing wrong, and {sibling} cannot forgive {N} for dragging the family through it. After that the family door stays shut.
fails: The letters go on for a year and split the family down the middle, and {N} is no longer welcome at the old house.

== the ward where it happened
tier: link
of_bold: a parent dies / U
side: well
delay: 1-2
holds: handling red tape
stages: juvenile+
age: 13-100
stakes: .6
tone: mixed
life: friends, health
horizon: months
roles: friend, sibling
earth: a friend's mother is dying on the ward where you lost a parent, and they ask you to help them through the forms and the meetings
scene: {friend} rings late. {friend}'s mother is on the same ward where {N} lost a parent, and {friend} does not know what to ask, what to sign or what the family is owed. {N} knows all of it now.
scene gone: {friend} has moved away, but writes: their mother is on a ward like the one {N} knows, far off, and {friend} needs to know what to ask for.
- W | go with them to every meeting, and see each form filled in properly | v: benevolence, conformity | act: go with the friend to every meeting, and see each form filled in properly | chance: 80
- U | write out for them everything you learned, step by step | v: benevolence, self-direction | act: write out for the friend everything they learned, step by step | chance: 85
- B | ring the people you got to know at the hospital, and get her seen first | v: power, benevolence | act: ring the people they got to know at the hospital, and get her seen first | chance: 70
- R | sit with them at the bedside through the nights, whatever else waits | v: benevolence | act: sit with the friend at the bedside through the nights, whatever else waits | chance: 80
- G | bring your own family round them, the way people gathered round yours | v: tradition, benevolence | act: bring their own family round the friend, the way people once gathered round them | chance: 75
works: {friend} gets through the forms and the meetings, and says later that {N} made it bearable.
works: The ward treats the family with care, and {friend} knows who to thank for it.
fails: Nothing {N} knows can change how it ends, and the old grief comes back hard.
fails: {friend} leans on {N} for months, and {N} is worn thin by it.
works gone: The family gets through the forms and the meetings, and later says {N} made it bearable.
works gone: The ward treats the family with care, and word reaches {N} of who they thank for it.
fails gone: Nothing {N} knows can change how it ends, and the old grief comes back hard.
fails gone: The letters and calls go on for months, and {N} is worn thin by them.

== bold: the ward where it happened / R
base: sit with them at the bedside through the nights, whatever else waits
likelier_if: has [home nursing] +10; has [calming people down] +5
- R | take the whole week off to be with them, whatever your boss says | v: benevolence, stimulation | act: take the whole week off to be with the friend, whatever the boss says | chance: 40 | grants: friend for life | drops_if_fails: kind:career
works: {N} is there every hour of that week, and {friend} says afterwards it is a debt no one could repay. They are friends for life from then on.
works: Through the long nights {N} and {friend} grow as close as family, and stay that way.
fails: The boss does not forgive the missed week, and {N} comes back to find the job gone.
fails: {N} loses the job over the missed shifts, and the week ends with a letter from work.
works gone: {N} spends the week on the long trip there and every hour after, and the old friend says it is a debt no one could repay. They are friends for life from then on.
works gone: Through that long week {N} and the old friend grow as close as family, across all the distance, and stay that way.
fails gone: The boss does not forgive the missed week, and {N} comes back to find the job gone.
fails gone: {N} loses the job over the missed shifts, and the week ends with a letter from work.

== clearing the old house
tier: link
of_bold: a parent dies / U
side: badly
delay: 1-3
stages: juvenile+
age: 13-100
stakes: .7
tone: trouble
life: family, home
horizon: weeks
roles: sibling, grandparent
earth: the family you fell out with over the hospital is clearing the old house, and you are told to come last
scene: The old house is being sold. {sibling} has told {N} to come on Saturday at four, after the others have taken what they want. Since the letters to the hospital, that is how things are in the family.
scene gone: {sibling} has moved away and left the house to an agent. {grandparent} rings {N}: the house goes on Monday, and whatever is left will be thrown out.
- W | come at four, as asked, and take only what was left for you | v: conformity | act: come at four, as asked, and take only what was left for them | chance: 85
- U | come early with the list of who was promised what, and go through it calmly | v: universalism, security | chance: 70
- B | ask the agent what the house will fetch, and what each of them will get | v: power | act: ask the agent what the house will fetch, and what each of the family will get | chance: 75
- R | go at noon with everyone else, and refuse to be sent away | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 65
- G | ask only for the plants in the garden, and dig them up yourself | v: tradition | act: ask only for the plants in the garden, and dig them up alone | chance: 80
works: {N} leaves with a box of things that matter, and {sibling} manages a nod at the gate.
works: The day passes without a row, and that is more than {N} hoped for.
fails: Words are said in the hallway that cannot be taken back.
fails: {N} arrives to find the rooms bare, and goes home with nothing.
works gone: {N} leaves with a box of things that matter, and nobody stands in the way.
works gone: The day passes quietly, and that is more than {N} hoped for.
fails gone: Nobody is there to argue with, and somehow that is worse.
fails gone: {N} arrives to find the rooms bare, and goes home with nothing.

== bold: clearing the old house / B
base: ask the agent what the house will fetch, and what each of them will get
likelier_if: has [good credit] +10; has [inheritance] +5
- B | put in your own offer for the house, against the agent's other buyers | v: power, security | act: put in their own offer for the house, against the agent's other buyers | chance: 35 | requires: savings | title: homeowner | takes_if_fails: savings
works: The offer wins. {N} holds the keys to the old house, and the family has to come to {Ns} door now.
works: The agent rings on Monday: the house is {Ns}, deposit paid and papers signed.
fails: The offer is beaten at the last minute, and the deposit and fees {N} had paid out are gone with it.
fails: The sale collapses after {N} has paid for the surveys and the deposit, and the savings are spent for nothing.

# ================================================================ earning a qualification

== bold: earning a qualification / B
base: use it at once to bargain for more: more money, more say, a better place
likelier_if: has [teachers' favourite] +10; has [mentor] +5; mark 'learned a skill' +5
- B | put in for the top scholarship there is, against the best of the year | v: achievement, power | act: put in for the top scholarship there is, against the best of the year | chance: 35 | grants: scholarship | drops_if_fails: kind:community
works: The letter comes in spring: the scholarship is {Ns}, fees and books and all.
works: {N} beats the best of the year to it, and the scholarship carries {N} on to the next course.
fails: {N} gives up the club and every evening to prepare, and still misses it. By then the place at the club has gone to someone else.
fails: The scholarship goes to {rival}. {N} had dropped out of the club to study for it, and the club does not keep the place.

