# ================================================================ losing a grandparent
works gone: The hardest paper suits {N} after all. The scholarship comes through, and the first letter {N} writes is to the old teacher.
works gone: A year of nights pays off, and {N} wins the scholarship on the paper nobody else would sit.
fails gone: {N} does badly on the hard paper, and the old teacher's letters, which once came every term, stop.
fails gone: The result is worse than last year's, and the old teacher turns to other students after that.

== bold: losing a grandparent / R
base: drop everything and go at once, to see them before the coffin is closed
likelier_if: has [passport] +10; has [second language] +10
- R | take their old ring back to where they were born, and find the family there | v: benevolence, stimulation | act: take the grandparent's old ring back to where they were born, and find the family there | chance: 40 | requires: savings | grants: family abroad | takes_if_fails: savings
works: In the town where {grandparent} was born, a houseful of cousins {N} never knew takes {N} in as one of their own.
works: The old family over the border opens its doors, and {N} comes home with addresses, photographs and promises to write.
fails: The journey eats every penny {N} had put by, and the relatives turn out to have moved on long ago.
fails: {N} spends all the savings getting there, and finds a shut house and neighbours who never heard the name.

